00:07:51.869 --> 00:07:54.006
Maybe that's 'cause of
my own personal prejudice

00:07:54.006 --> 00:07:56.687
of being someone who struggled
learning another one,

00:07:56.687 --> 00:07:59.252
even though I got two from
at least a hearing standpoint

00:07:59.252 --> 00:08:00.413
and I can communicate.

00:08:00.413 --> 00:08:01.713
You throw me in Moscow for a month,

00:08:01.713 --> 00:08:03.827
that Russian you just heard
will get a hell of a lot better

00:08:03.827 --> 00:08:06.171
as my ear and tongue get adapted to it.

00:08:06.171 --> 00:08:07.623
I also think technology is now coming

00:08:07.623 --> 00:08:09.190
where we're gonna be able to translate,

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:11.628
clearly, in a decade, I'll
be able to go to China

00:08:11.628 --> 00:08:14.426
and just be like, or like talk into here

00:08:14.426 --> 00:08:16.991
or just, it's in it, or
put in the ear pieces.

00:08:16.991 --> 00:08:19.603
Does anybody not know that we're gonna put

00:08:19.603 --> 00:08:21.391
ear pieces in when we
go to foreign countries

00:08:21.391 --> 00:08:22.726
