gonna talk our languages

00:08:22.726 --> 00:08:25.790
and everything's gonna
be translated proper?

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:29.830
And so the value I put on it has gone down

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:33.604
in value as I recognize
technology's gonna fix that issue.

00:08:33.604 --> 00:08:36.414
- [Voiceover] Benjamin asks,
"Gary, I want to start pushing

00:08:36.414 --> 00:08:38.655
"people to make the same decision I made

00:08:38.655 --> 00:08:41.592
"by leaving a very secure
job to pursue their dream.

00:08:41.592 --> 00:08:45.295
"My question is, will my
employee retention rate drop?

00:08:45.295 --> 00:08:47.768
"Since you started building
up your personal brand,

00:08:47.768 --> 00:08:51.228
"has your employee
retention rate dropped?"

00:08:51.228 --> 00:08:53.654
- Benjamin, the thing you
need to understand is that

00:08:53.654 --> 00:08:55.570
intent trumps everything.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:58.912
And so I think one amazing
thing in this company

00:08:58.912 --> 00:09:01.815
that I'm extremely proud
of is I truly believe

00:09:01.815 --> 00:09:04.926
that these people that
work at VaynerMedia

00:09:04.926 --> 00:09:08.305
really recognize that I want to win

00:09:08.305 --> 00:09:09.744
but not at their expense.

00:09:09.744 --> 00:09:12.670
I want to buy the Jets, not at
the expense of my employees,

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:16.350
with my employees and I equally
want what's best for them.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:18.509
Of course, you know,
looking at these three,

00:09:18.509 --> 00:09:20.772
and things are running through my mind

00:09:20.772 --> 00:09:23.872
and, obviously, I know them
all at different levels,

00:09:23.872 --> 00:09:26.229
but you know, there's
narratives in my mind

00:09:26.229 --> 00:09:29.235
that I can play out right
now that leads to a world

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:30.826
of them not being here.

00:09:30.826 --> 00:09:32.289
And that makes me sad and I really

00:09:32.289 --> 00:09:33.193
don't want that.

00:09:33.193 --> 00:09:35.771
And from an ego standpoint,
I truly believe that I

00:09:35.771 --> 00:09:38.754
can bring them so much
value over the long haul

00:09:38.754 --> 00:09:40.913
that makes it interesting
for them to stay.

00:09:40.913 --> 00:09:44.292
But I think it's massively
important that they always,

00:09:44.292 --> 00:09:48.007
deep down, feel as though I want them

00:09:48.007 --> 00:09:50.085
to have what they want,

00:09:50.085 --> 00:09:52.673
even though, optically,
it doesn't benefit me.

00:09:52.673 --> 00:09:55.483
And I would say 40% of
VaynerMedia believes that.

00:09:55.483 --> 00:09:57.248
And that may surprise you as a low number,

00:09:57.248 --> 00:09:59.326
but I hope you understand
the level of cynicism

00:09:59.326 --> 00:10:01.543
that is instilled in us as human beings

00:10:01.543 --> 00:10:03.772
to not believe everything I just said.

00:10:03.772 --> 00:10:05.827
And so I'm massively proud of the 40%

00:10:05.827 --> 00:10:08.067
and I'm really pumped
that I think that 40%

00:10:08.067 --> 00:10:10.807
was actually 12% only 12 to 18 months ago

00:10:10.807 --> 00:10:13.129
and so I'm building momentum, right?

00:10:13.129 --> 00:10:15.962
Look, I think if you're
scared to lose somebody

00:10:15.962 --> 00:10:17.947
who believes in their heart that they have

00:10:17.947 --> 00:10:19.363
the skill set to go and do it,

00:10:19.363 --> 00:10:21.870
you're making a huge
mistake and I actually think

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:25.585
you build retention by
showing them the reverse.

00:10:25.585 --> 00:10:29.091
It's a reverse psychology
game that is not a tactic

00:10:29.091 --> 00:10:30.449
because if you don't actually believe it,

00:10:30.449 --> 00:10:32.550
that reverse psychology
will come across as bullshit

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:33.526
and you'll lose it.

00:10:33.526 --> 00:10:35.941
I don't do it because I want
to reverse psychology India,

00:10:35.941 --> 00:10:38.065
I do it because I believe it.

00:10:38.065 --> 00:10:41.025
And then they have to believe
and evolve in their place.

00:10:41.025 --> 00:10:43.963
You know, I believe that
the evolution of people

00:10:43.963 --> 00:10:45.646
not being here is gonna
have a lot more to do

00:10:45.646 --> 00:10:48.223
with things in life, they
fall in love and get married,

00:10:48.223 --> 00:10:50.800
and have to move 'cause
their spouse really needs

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.459
to do this and they have
the empathy and being

00:10:53.459 --> 00:10:54.840
the bigger man or woman
in the relationship

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:56.409
to go let their spouse do that,

00:10:56.409 --> 00:10:59.286
unfortunately, maybe something tragic.

00:10:59.286 --> 00:11:02.641
I actually think that when you're pure,

00:11:02.641 --> 00:11:04.847
when you want to win but
you want to win with,

00:11:04.847 --> 00:11:07.865
not, you know, on the
back of, people start

00:11:07.865 --> 00:11:09.827
sticking around because the truth is,

00:11:09.827 --> 00:11:12.579
if somebody works at a
job, in a lot of ways,

00:11:12.579 --> 00:11:15.666
they weren't thinking
purely, I'm gonna put this

00:11:15.666 --> 00:11:17.037
on my back to begin with, right?

00:11:17.037 --> 00:11:19.057
And you, and I don't know your age,

00:11:19.057 --> 00:11:21.076
is there a picture, or
is this a written word?

